MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cluster A (missing setter value): the reflective DataView proto-member body and
the closed-method dispatcher both padded an ABSENT argument with
`ref.null.extern`. Standalone tells `null` and `undefined` apart, so
ToNumber(pad) was 0 where ToNumber(undefined) = NaN is required — `setFloat32()`
wrote 0. Both sites now pad with the canonical `undefined` singleton, and the
BigInt setters' ToBigInt(undefined) TypeError switches from a bare `ref.is_null`
to a nullish-OR-undefined test so it keeps firing.

Cluster F (module-global view): `var ta = new Uint8Array(buffer, 0)` at MODULE
scope got the checker-inferred plain TypedArray vec as its global slot type, so
the shared-backing `$__ta_view` the constructor emits failed the slot and the
global stayed null — every later `ta[i]` / `ta.length` threw "Cannot access
property on null or undefined". Function-local let/const slots already consulted
`inferTaViewType` (#4376); module globals now do too, and the two receiver
lookups that were locals-only (`taViewReceiverTypeIdx`, the `.length` arm of
`tryLengthAndNameReads`) also consult module globals. test262 declares every
binding at top level, which is why the whole `DataView/prototype/set*` family
was blocked on this.

Also lands the two explicit-`undefined` externref tests and the shared
`isViewRefTestInstrs` carrier chain that the later clusters build on.

