From: =?UTF-8?q?Thomas=20Tr=C3=A4nkler?= <git@thomas.traenkler.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:21:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] =?UTF-8?q?fix(#5150):=20cluster=20G=20=E2=80=94=20Arr?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ayBuffer.isView=20as=20a=20first-class=20value?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`var isView = ArrayBuffer.isView; isView(x)` fell to the generic
"ArrayBuffer.isView is not yet implemented in --target standalone" throw: only
the DIRECT call site had a host-free lowering. The value read now mints the same
1-arg boxed-predicate closure the `Number.is*` family uses, whose body is the
carrier `ref.test` chain — shared with the direct call through
`isViewRefTestInstrs` (dataview-native.ts) so the two can never drift apart.

The shared chain also gained the `$__ta_view` carriers. A buffer-backed
`new Uint8Array(buffer)` is a shared-backing view struct, not one of the plain
`$Vec`s, so the pre-existing chain answered `false` for it whenever the static
type could not decide — which is always, for a value read.

The known imprecision is unchanged and still documented at the helper:
standalone shares the `$Vec` carrier between `number[]` and TypedArrays, so a
plain array reads as a view. That is the accepted price of not emitting the
`__arraybuffer_isView` host import, which would break the whole module at
instantiate. The `isView/arg-is-typedarray*.js` rows remain failing for the
separate reason that their harness constructs through a TypedArray ctor VALUE.

